  "details": "If I understand correctly, visemes work by taking the shape keys that are assigned to each mouth movement and are gradually played from values \"0 to 100\" to create a smooth, realistic transition between each sound. Personally it seems more like a \"0 to 80\" perhaps. Or maybe that's just my experience? But hey every avatar is different, so it should be customizable. My current avatar would benefit from an instantaneous viseme change (0 and then 100, no transition) because I use several 2D images that switch back and forth for my mouth movements as opposed to a 3D mesh morphing. The current viseme feature causes my mouth movements to overlap and some movements only want to come out part of the way. I would greatly appreciate having a feature to customize the viseme shape key values or an override of some sort for visemes!",
